===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|winbrā}}, {{m|gmh|wintprā}}, variants of {{inh|de|gmh|wintbrā}}, {{m|gmh|wintbrāwe}}, from {{inh|de|goh|wintbrāwa}}, from {{com|goh|wint|brāwa|nocat=1}}; see {{m|de|Braue}} for the second component. It has been theorised that the first component may be cognate with {{cog|prg|wanso||first hairs on the face}} and thence with {{cog|ru|усы||moustache}}, as well as {{cog|grc|ἴονθος||downy hair}} and {{cog|mga|find||hair}}, all from {{der|de|ine-pro|*wendʰ-||to wind, to turn}}, with "hair" being derived from the original "winding up and down" meaning.

